WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.596
With next-intl, your app renders
translations that a team or

2
00:00:04.596 --> 00:00:06.546
a service writes into a catalog.

3
00:00:06.946 --> 00:00:10.011
It supports the App Router
and Server Components,

4
00:00:10.011 --> 00:00:11.763
under the MIT license.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.180
General Translation writes the
translations for your catalogs

6
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.781
or inline JSX.

7
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.620
Keep next-intl, and the gt CLI
translates its catalogs without

8
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.873
touching your components.

9
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.235
Or move to gt-next, and write
each heading inside a T component.

10
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:34.039
Either way, npx gt translate
writes the German translation

11
00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:35.175
before your build.

12
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.855
Your team now ships
German with each release.
